@fm description | description | How the crew of Crumbwick Bakery opens the shop before the first customer arrives.
# Opening the shop
s description | The opening crew arrives at half past five and works until the doors open at seven.
s description | Every morning follows the same order, and the order matters more than the speed.
## Lamps and doors
s gate{open_lamps} | Switch on the front lamps before you unlock the street door.
s rule{open_key} | Unlock the street door with the brass key that hangs in the sconce room.
s prohibition{open_back} | Never prop the back door open with a crate while the ovens are warm.
s description | The sconce room is the small cupboard behind the till, and it holds every key.
s gate | Check that the alarm panel shows a green light, then write the time in the opening book.
s example | For example, if the panel shows an amber light, the night crew left a window open.
## Ovens
s gate{open_ovens} | Light the big oven first and the small oven ten minutes later.
s gate{open_preheat} | Wait until the big oven reads two hundred and twenty degrees before the first tray goes in.
s description | The big oven holds twelve trays and the small oven holds four.
s prohibition | Do not load a cold tray into a hot oven, because the glaze will crack.
s example | Case: a tray of pinnocks went in cold on a Monday and came out with split tops.
## The dough loft
l rule{open_loft} | Carry the proved dough down from the dough loft in the wheeled bin
l gate | Weigh each pinnock on the brass scale before it is shaped
l prohibition | Do not stack more than three bins on the lift
l description | The loft is warmest near the east window
## Final checks
s gate | Count the float in the till before you open the street door.
s rule | Fill the front shelves from left to right, oldest loaves first.
s description | Customers usually form a line by ten past seven.
s none | Thank you for opening well.
s none | Good luck today.
